    "['flexible-vlan-tagging', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS command for the Juniper `set interfaces ge-1/0/0 flexible-vlan-tagging` configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q\\n switchport mode trunk\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this isn't a direct 1:1 translation (as flexible-vlan-tagging is a Juniper-specific concept), this Cisco configuration achieves similar functionality by:\\n1. Enabling 802.1Q trunking\\n2. Setting the interface to trunk mode\\n3. Implicitly allowing multiple VLANs (similar to Juniper's flexible-vlan-tagging)\\n\\nThe Cisco configuration is more explicit about the trunking protocol (dot1q) compared to Juniper's more abstract approach.\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS command for the Juniper `set interfaces ge-1/0/0 flexible-vlan-tagging` configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q\\n switchport mode trunk\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this isn't a direct 1:1 translation (as flexible-vlan-tagging is a Juniper-specific concept), this Cisco configuration achieves similar functionality by:\\n1. Enabling 802.1Q trunking\\n2. Setting the interface to trunk mode\\n3. Implicitly allowing multiple VLANs (similar to Juniper's flexible-vlan-tagging)\\n\\nThe Cisco configuration is more explicit about the trunking protocol (dot1q) compared to Juniper's more abstract approach.\", 'trans_template': 'switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'switchport mode trunk', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface rang